<p>Pope Leo XIV led his first Easter Vigil in St. Peter’s Basilica at the Vatican on April 4, carrying a lit candle into the darkened basilica as Catholics began one of Christianity’s central celebrations. In his homily, he urged people not to grow numb to the scale of wars around the world and called on the faithful to help rebuild bonds broken by war, injustice, and the isolation of peoples and nations. That appeal put peace at the center of Leo’s first Easter season as pope. The articles note that he has repeatedly called for an end to hostilities amid the US-Israeli war on Iran and Russia’s continuing campaign in Ukraine. The service also carried a hopeful message: at a moment of global conflict, the pope used Christianity’s most joyful feast to encourage harmony, human connection, and a practical commitment to peace everywhere.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/GzFlHTH-mhxgw_KETrHkBZ2Xcn6dM0Jg_-cSlbmsOOi-Nm4QHq1XgsKJEvGSSZs5jWmqoCbY0ajW2baendlihMhHE4Je0HSduwSy9hnAj6lUTBQrKxvOfnuGbwVs_vXioa0ztBWt2YDZd0-nUypH5Mhh8Ye-1uwWbKjQVHCzmllDbsnhJt29GuAQSgum54LHDlGDqWSbWprpl1uY5JOCFAMn3LboFa8_lS11fBBLulHIf-_gNK-hbYi5QNzXBpncDXxSW5gcUHxe1eOgcg' alt='Pope Leo XIV waves after leading the Easter Vigil inside St. Peter&#x27;s Basilica at The Vatican, Saturday, April 4, 2026. (AP Photo/Andrew Medichini)' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Palm Sunday: On Palm Sunday, Leo said God does not listen to the prayers of people who make war or invoke God to justify violence.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo XIV: Leo urged believers to commit to bringing peace and harmony &quot;everywhere and always throughout the world,&quot; presenting peace as an active duty rather than a passive wish. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/religions/article/2026/04/05/during-pope-leo-xiv-s-first-easter-vigil-a-call-for-harmony-and-peace-in-a-war-torn-world_6752124_63.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Reuters reporting via Al-Monitor: The coverage portrayed Leo as an outspoken critic of the Iran war and highlighted his warning that fear and mistrust are fraying human ties across nations. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/easter-vigil-pope-leo-urges-world-not-grow-numb-war'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>The Globe and Mail: Its report linked the vigil to Leo’s earlier Palm Sunday message that religious language must not be used to justify violence. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-pope-leo-easter-vigil-peace-world-at-war/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/easter-vigil-pope-leo-urges-world-not-grow-numb-war'>At Easter vigil, Pope Leo urges world not to grow numb to war</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-pope-leo-easter-vigil-peace-world-at-war/'>Pope Leo XIV celebrates first Easter vigil, calls for peace in world torn by war</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-first-easter-vigil-calls-for-harmony-and-peace-in-a-world-torn-by-war'>Pope Leo XIV celebrates first Easter vigil, calls for harmony and peace in a world torn by war</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/religions/article/2026/04/05/during-pope-leo-xiv-s-first-easter-vigil-a-call-for-harmony-and-peace-in-a-war-torn-world_6752124_63.html'>During Pope Leo XIV&#x27;s first Easter vigil, a call for harmony and peace in a war-torn world</a> - lemonde.fr</li></ul>